{"name":"Wisdom","hex":"#e2e3d8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Wisdom","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The Wisdom of Solomon, a book of the Catholic and Eastern Orthodox canon of the Old Testament, considered apocryphal by Protestants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Wisdom"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wisdom","blocks":[{"text":"Wisdom, also known as sapience, is defined by psychologists as a combination of \"wit and virtue,\" the ability to apply expert tacit and experiential knowledge, balancing intrapersonal, interpersonal and institutional interests, to deal with complex questions of life and attain a common good. Wisdom can be viewed as a stable personality trait, but also as context-bound process, meaning that a person in some contexts behaves wisely, but in other contexts does not. Wisdom can also be viewed as influenced and determined by sociocultural norms and traditions. Wisdom can be viewed solely as wise behaviour, describing actions which lead to \"an altruistic outcome by creatively and successfully solving problems.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Luca_Giordano_-_Dream_of_Solomon_-_WGA09004.jpg/330px-Luca_Giordano_-_Dream_of_Solomon_-_WGA09004.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wisdom"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Center_detail%2C_from-_Interior_of_a_Book_Cover-_Manjuvajra_Embracing_His_Consort%2C_with_Attendant_Lamas_MET_DP335604_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Center_detail%2C_from-_Interior_of_a_Book_Cover-_Manjuvajra_Embracing_His_Consort%2C_with_Attendant_Lamas_MET_DP335604_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Center_detail%2C_from-_Interior_of_a_Book_Cover-_Manjuvajra_Embracing_His_Consort%2C_with_Attendant_Lamas_M